("p", "The copying reaction is **not perfectly accurate**. Small errors produce **variations**. If every copy were exactly the same, a sudden change in the environment (heat, a new disease or a shortage of food) could wipe out the entire population. Variations give some individuals a chance to survive, and these pass the useful features to their offspring."),
